        "comments": "This project provides (pseudo-)haplotype two of the diploid genome assembly of the burbot, Lota lota with a sample provided by Kim Prabel. The data generation and assembly were carried out by EBP-Nor (https://www.ebpnor.org/). The fLotLot1.1 assembly is based on 46x PromethION R10 Oxford Nanopore and 125x Arima Hi-C data. The ONT reads were assembled with hifiasm along with Hi-C data to generate a pair of haplotype-resolved assemblies. K-mers from the two assemblies were used to filter Hi-C reads to create two sets of reads for scaffolding the assemblies (i.e., reads used to scaffold hap1 did not contain k-mers unique to hap2). YaHS was used for scaffolding. FCS-adaptor was used to remove putative adapters, and putative contaminants were removed with FCS-GX. The chromosomes are named according to size.",
